-- **Constraints block.** A Goal body's constraints block runs from the first line that starts with `May change:`, `Read only:` or `Never:` to the end of the body. It is valid when it holds each of the three headings and every non-empty line in it starts with one of them. Replay stores no word for it and no status reads it. `hyp add goal` admits any body and warns when the body has a heading but no valid block. `hyp prompt G --actor A` prints the `/goal` prompt for G from G's node and the store's place in its repository: the store's path relative to the repository root, A, G, the skill hyp-goal-run, the stop clauses, and each block line as written, in body order; `--branch` and `--pr` add a clause each after the block. It refuses with exit 1 and nothing on stdout when the block is missing or not valid, naming each problem, and exits 2 with no `--actor` (it does not read `$HYP_ACTOR`), for an id that is not a Goal, or for a `--branch` that holds a space or a control character. It exits 3 when no repository holds the store. A line is empty only when it holds no byte, so a line of spaces inside the block is a bad line. It reads no answer, so the same Goal and flags print the same bytes before and after an answer and in a store with other Goals.
